WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.800
Welcome to the British Council 
Learning Hub

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.120
When it comes to teaching English 
to young children

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.120
our priority is to turn their
curiosity

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.760
into confidence

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.760
that's why we've introduced the
British Council Learning Hub

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.000
as part of their Primary Plus course

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.440
It's a safe and secure online space

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:25.200
where your child can continue their
English language learning adventure

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.600
at home

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.520
and it's a new way

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.840
New Caption

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.840
New Caption

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:37.720
to suit your child's age 
and personal development

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.720
so that they can complete 
them independently

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:46.112
First you'll find all the information 
you need

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.814
to activate your child's account

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.482
in your welcome email

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:53.720
We have another video to guide you 
through the process if you need more help

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:58.320
Once logged on your child will choose
the module they're working on

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.080
and press open

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.000
welcome to Yummy!

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.880
a module from Primary Plus 1

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:05.600
it's all about food

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:08.399
First we want to show you
the features

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.199
that give parents a window into
the classroom

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.066
Such as your child's magazine

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.840
You'll find it in the resources section

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:22.474
This is what your child will use in class
with their teacher and classmates

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:25.160
There is one for every module

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:31.280
Let's see how you can track
your child's progress

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.800
You and your child will find the
progress dashboard

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.520
in the about this module section

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:40.786
Together you can celebrate your
child's successes

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.600
and encourage them with areas
for improvement

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:47.640
There are up to 10 activities 
per module

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:50.640
that get more challenging as
your child progresses

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.239
 te 

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.440
Your child will find activities

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:58.038
in the first two sections

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:01.807
then songs and videos in sections
3 and 4

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.680
So let's show you some activities

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.946
Let's choose the Do you like 
listening game

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:11.560
Here your child needs to match
what they hear

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:13.280
with the correct pictures

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.280
first they need to click on the 
speakerphone icon

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.080
to listen to the narrator say

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.560
whether or not they like a certain
food

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:24.844
Do you like milk?

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.485
Yes I do

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:31.240
Your child then needs to decide
which of the four pictures

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.245
best matches what they've heard

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.320
New Caption

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:38.160
Once your child has finished

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.360
They can close the tab by clicking 
on the X in the top right hand corner

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.800
Now let's try the Colour grouping
game

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:49.920
designed to help your child improve
their listening and reading skills

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.880
Here your child needs to group

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.360
words associated with certain
mealtimes

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.640
By clicking on the speakerphone
icon

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.680
your child will listen to the narrator 
say

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.278
during which mealtime

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.345
they eat certain foods

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.753
For breakfast I like cereal

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.240
Your child needs to click
the paintbrush

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:12.320
in the pink paint

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:16.240
then select the foods the narrator 
says they eat for breakfast

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.000
they can click on the green paint

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.360
to switch colours

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.800
then paint the foods the narrator eats

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:22.998
for lunch

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.232
finally they press finish

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:29.800
Songs make listening practice
fun for your child

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:32.299
This song is from the weather
module

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:36.000
First your child needs to read 
the sentences

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.898
That are listed in the wrong 
order

00:03:39.586 --> 00:03:41.920
You can hear the song by clicking 
on the play button

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.280
They need to listen out for
the sentences

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.646
So that they can list them in the
right order

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:49.760
They can also click on and read
the transcript

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:50.991
below the video

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:58.800
To complete the activity

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.880
they need to click once on the
sentence they want to move

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.880
Then once on the sentence they
want to replace

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:09.073
They can click finish to see if they 
have made the correct choices

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.606
If not they can try again

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.760
Like in classes

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:17.192
Our partnership with academy
award winning

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:18.800
animation studio Aardman

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.320
helps us bring English
learning to life

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.080
to keep your child engaged

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:25.600
When your child completes
their activities

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:29.067
they can watch a Shaun the Sheep
video as a reward for their efforts

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.640
When your child moves up to
Primary Plus 3

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:35.240
they will enjoy learning with 
even more stimulating activities

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:38.240
that they can do before and after
class

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.840
This new approach will help
them feel

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.160
more prepared

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:43.680
free up more time in class
for speaking

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:45.478
build up their confidence

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:47.600
and enable them to make
more progress

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:50.080
in the English language 
learning journey

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:52.280
There really is a lot to look
forward to

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:53.444
Bye

